# =============================================================================
# Step-3.7-Flash -- Unsloth Dynamic Q8_K_XL
# =============================================================================
# Same architecture as the Q4 profile, ~195 GiB on disk (6 shards) vs ~114.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-25, 262144 context, --fit, GPU idle):
#   generation  ~13 tok/s     (exactly half of Q4_K_XL's ~26)
#   prefill     ~141 tok/s    (vs Q4's ~250)
# --fit places ~13 expert layers on the GPU and ~29 in system RAM (vs ~20/22
# for Q4), so each token reads ~2x the bytes over DDR5 -- hence ~half the speed.
# Coherent output confirmed; use this as a QUALITY reference, not for daily use.
# Unsloth's dynamic Q4_K_XL already keeps the quality-critical tensors high, so
# Q4_K_XL is the better default for almost everything.
#
#   ./serve.sh step-3.7-flash-q8
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

: "${IK_MODEL_GLOB:=${IK_MODELS_ROOT}/unsloth/Step-3.7-Flash-GGUF/Step-3.7-Flash-UD-Q8_K_XL-00001-of-*.gguf}"

: "${IK_ALIAS:=step-3.7-flash-q8}"

# Full context, matching the Q4 default. This loads and runs at 262144 (~24 GiB
# KV cache); --fit hands the rest of VRAM to experts. Lower it to trade context
# for a bit more generation speed, exactly as with Q4 (see docs/TUNING.md §3).
: "${IK_CTX:=262144}"

# --fit rather than a hand-picked -ncmoe: with ~29 layers already forced onto
# the CPU there is little to gain from squeezing one more onto the GPU (~13 ->
# ~14 tok/s), so the auto-fit split is left to do the safe thing. A little extra
# margin because the model is so much larger than VRAM.
: "${IK_FIT_MARGIN:=3072}"

# ~155 GiB of q8 experts live in system RAM. -rtr speeds up PREFILL (measured
# +16% on Q4; likely more here with more CPU layers) but not generation, and it
# forces --no-mmap so every start re-reads ~195 GiB from disk. Only worth it for
# prefill-heavy use; for the gain without the startup cost, repack the file once
# with llama-quantize --repack. Benchmark: ./bench.sh rtr step-3.7-flash-q8
: "${IK_RTR:=0}"

# Note: at 195 GiB the model nearly fills the 224 GiB of RAM once the CPU-side
# experts are resident. Close other big memory users before serving Q8.
